    <sys:String x:Key="TaskPlan_SpHelpTitle">Task Plan with SharePoint — step by step</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="TaskPlan_SpHelpIntro">The recommended way to use a SharePoint sheet is to sync it to a local folder with OneDrive.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="TaskPlan_SpHelpStep1">In the browser, open the SharePoint library that holds the sheet, for example the project site's Documents library.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="TaskPlan_SpHelpStep2">Click "Sync" or "Add shortcut to OneDrive" in the library toolbar.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="TaskPlan_SpHelpStep3">Windows creates a synced local folder. It shows up in Explorer under your organization.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="TaskPlan_SpHelpStep4">In Task Plan, use Open and pick the .xlsx file inside that synced folder. Do not paste the browser's https:// link.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="TaskPlan_SpHelpStep5">When you save in Task Plan, OneDrive pushes the change to SharePoint automatically and everyone syncing the same library receives the new version.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="TaskPlan_SpHelpWarning">Important: avoid editing the sheet in Excel Online and Task Plan at the same time. The file may get locked or create version conflicts.</sys:String>
