    <sys:String x:Key="SU_Title">How to use the schedule</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_Sub">Use the grid and the Gantt to plan dates, duration, progress, resources and sprints. NXProject recalculates activity finish dates from the work calendar.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_1H">1. Duration (Dur.(h))</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_1P">The Dur.(h) column works in real effort hours, not calendar time. Enter 8 for 8 hours, 16.5 for 16 hours and 30 minutes.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_1a">- To convert working days into hours, use the d suffix: 2d becomes 2 working days.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_1b">- Changing Dur.(h) recalculates the Finish date, keeping the Start date and applying the resource allocation %.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_1c">- When Current HH is greater than 0, the displayed duration is Current HH + Remaining HH.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_1d">- The allocation % does not change the HH: 40h stays 40h. It changes how many calendar days those hours span.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_1e">- Duration editing is locked when the activity is 100% complete.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_2H">2. Current HH and Remaining HH</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_2P">Current HH is the effort already done on the activity. Remaining HH is the effort still needed to complete it.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_2a">- Total duration = Current HH + Remaining HH (when Current HH is filled in).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_2b">- When you change % Compl., NXProject automatically recalculates Current HH and Remaining HH.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_2c">- These fields are synced with Azure DevOps (HH_Atual_float and HH_Restante_float fields).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_2d">- To view the columns, use View, Customize columns and enable Current HH and Remaining HH.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_3H">3. Completion percentage (% Compl.)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_3P">When you type the completion percentage, NXProject recalculates Current HH and Remaining HH proportionally to the activity's total duration.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_3a">- With % = 100, Current HH takes the total duration and Remaining HH becomes zero; if Start + duration falls in the future, Finish is capped at today. Exception: if Start is fixed in the future, Finish equals the fixed Start.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_3b">- When registering the first progress (% 0 to above 0): if the Start date is in the future, it is moved to today, anchoring the activity start.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_3c">- Once the activity has started (% above 0), the Start date is no longer changed by the cascade — only the following activities of the same resource are repositioned.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_3d">- Any % change that moves the Finish date triggers the virtual predecessor cascade for the following activities.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_3e">- Activities in the Closed state with % other than 100 still have editable duration.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_4H">4. Start and Finish dates</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_4P">The Finish date is calculated automatically: Start + real HH converted by the allocation %, respecting the calendar (weekends and holidays are skipped).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_4a">- Changing the Finish date changes the duration; the system asks for confirmation before accepting.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_4b">- Typing 0 in the Start field removes the pin and repositions by sprint or predecessor.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_4c">- The calendar setup is under View, Calendar.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_5H">5. Explicit predecessors</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_5P">The Pred. column defines which activities must finish before the current activity starts.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_5a">- Click the Pred. field to open the selection window.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_5b">- Use search to find by name or ID.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_5c">- You can check multiple predecessors with the checkboxes.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_5d">- The start date is calculated automatically as the next working day after the latest finish date among all predecessors.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_5e">- When a predecessor's finish date changes, all dependents are recalculated in cascade.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_5f">- The recalculation uses topological sorting: an activity is only recalculated after all its predecessors are positioned. Cross references (A depends on B which depends on A) are detected and interrupted automatically.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_6H">6. Schedule milestones</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_6P">Milestones are zero-duration activities used to record an important date in the schedule.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_6a">- For a local milestone that does not go to Azure DevOps, use Type = No DevOps and Dur.(h) = 0.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_6b">- For a milestone that syncs to Azure DevOps, use Type = Marco-Devops and Dur.(h) = 0; it is created as a Task with the MARCO-PROJECT tag.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_6c">- Marco-Devops only accepts zero duration. Regular DevOps activities do not accept zero duration as a milestone.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_6d">- If the milestone has explicit predecessors, the start date uses the latest finish date among them, as with other activities.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_6e">- If the Marco-Devops has no predecessor set, the system automatically uses the previous sibling activity; if there is no previous sibling, it uses the parent.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_6f">- On Azure DevOps import, the Marco-Devops is positioned by the predecessor that makes sense in the hierarchy: a sibling activity or the parent itself.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_6g">- Predecessors outside the hierarchy may exist as a DevOps dependency, but are ignored when positioning the milestone visually within the list.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_7H">7. Gantt</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_7P">The Gantt shows duration bars, milestones, sprints and dependency arrows.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_7a">- The light blue bar represents the activity's total planned duration.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_7b">- The dark central band represents the % complete, reading similarly to MS Project.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_7c">- The subtle dark line at the base represents Current HH proportional to the total of Current HH + Remaining HH.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_7d">- The light gray-blue bar represents groupings such as Feature or Epic.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_7e">- Enable the magnifier button on the toolbar and move the mouse over the Gantt to analyze the chart up close.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_7f">- When moving an activity in the Gantt, dependents may follow the shift.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_8H">8. Columns and display modes</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_8P">Use the View, Customize columns button to choose which columns appear in each view mode.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_8a">- Standard view: compact setup, ideal for smaller monitors.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_8b">- Expanded view: full setup with Current HH, Remaining HH, OrgH, SFP and Predecessors.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_8c">- The setup is saved in the project file and restored when reopened.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_9H">9. Project Progress and S-Curve</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_9P">Access via View, Project Progress and S-Curve to track the project's overall progress.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_9a">- Blue line: Original HH (Planned) accumulated per sprint.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_9b">- Solid orange line: accumulated Current HH (completed or ongoing sprints).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_9c">- Dashed orange line: projected Remaining HH (future sprints).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_9d">- The calculation considers only activities at the story level (the shallowest level with an assigned sprint).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_10H">10. Virtual Predecessor (same resource and hierarchy)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_10P">Activities at the same hierarchy level with the same assigned resource are chained automatically, as if the previous activity were the predecessor of the next — without registering explicit predecessors.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_10a">- The chaining follows the order of activities in the list within the same level and same parent.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_10b">- When an activity's finish date changes, the following ones of the same resource and level are recalculated in cascade.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_10c">- The recalculation happens when changing duration, start date, finish date, completion percentage, explicit predecessor or resource.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_10d">- When changing the resource, the activity is repositioned after the last activity of the new resource at the same level; the previous resource's activities are also readjusted.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_10e">- When dragging an activity to another position, dates are recalculated at both the source and destination positions.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_10f">- Activities with explicit predecessors are not moved by the virtual predecessor.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_10g">- When opening or importing the project, virtual chaining and explicit predecessors are applied automatically across the whole hierarchy.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_11H">11. Sprint</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_11P">The Sprint column links the activity to an Azure DevOps iteration (or to a synthetic schedule sprint number).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_11a">- When changing the sprint of an activity with no progress (% = 0), the start date is moved to the start of the selected sprint and the finish is recalculated by duration.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_11b">- If the activity already has progress (% above 0), the start date is preserved; only the finish is recalculated keeping the current duration.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_11c">- When changing the sprint, the ancestors' dates (Feature, Epic, Project) are recalculated automatically to reflect the new range of the set of child activities.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_11d">- Changing the sprint does not cause a full grid refresh: only the activity's row and its ancestors are updated, preserving scroll position and selection.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_Tip">Quick tip: enter Start and Dur.(h) — the Finish is computed from the calendar. Activities of the same resource and level chain automatically. Update % Compl. to record progress; Current HH and Remaining HH are computed and synced with Azure DevOps.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="SU_Close">Close</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_Title">Azure DevOps Backlog Integration</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_Header">Integration with Azure DevOps Backlog</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_Sub">Use Azure DevOps as the backlog source and NXProject as support for schedule, Gantt, sprints, capacity and deadline tracking.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_1H">1. Prepare the backlog in Azure DevOps</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_1P">The root work item entered in NXProject must represent the project and contain the backlog hierarchy below it.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_1a">- Project - the planning root item.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_1b">- Epic and Feature - group larger deliverables.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_1c">- Story - becomes the plannable schedule row.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_2H">2. Configure fields used in the schedule</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_2P">In the File, Import, TFS / Azure DevOps window, enter the organization, the Team Project, the root ID and the Personal Access Token. In the advanced fields area, adjust the names used by your process.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_2a">- HH Estimado: the Story estimate in hours.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_2b">- Data_Inicio: start date when the Story already has an agreed start.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_2c">- Data_Fim: finish date when the deadline is already set in DevOps.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_2d">- System.AssignedTo: assignee imported as a project resource.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_3H">3. Work with sprints and backlog order</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_3P">NXProject reads Azure DevOps iterations and uses System.IterationPath to associate Features and Stories to sprints. The order among sibling items respects Microsoft.VSTS.Common.StackRank, keeping the backlog sense for planning.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_3P2">After import, changing the sprint in the grid can be synced back to Azure DevOps.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_4H">4. Track agile projects with NXProject</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_4a">- Gantt to see dates, dependencies and impact among Stories.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_4b">- Allocation by resource and sprint to assess team capacity.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_4c">- Health Check to identify delays and follow the S-Curve.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_4d">- Block tags on child Tasks indicate a visual block in planning.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_5H">5. Sync carefully</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_5P">In File, Export, Sync TFS / Azure DevOps, NXProject updates linked work items according to the integration rules.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_5a">- Can send title, description, hours, dates, state, tags and sprint.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_5b">- Can create new items when the DevOps ID is 0 and a type is defined.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_5c">- Can sync predecessor links if the option is enabled.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_5d">- Before syncing, review assignees, 100% complete items and Stories without a sprint.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_Tip">Summary: the backlog stays in Azure DevOps; NXProject complements it with visual planning, capacity, dates and dependencies to support agile projects.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="ADO_Close">Close</sys:String>

</ResourceDictionary>
